# Section & View Layout

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A dashboard view arranges its cards in one of four ways. The view type decides the layout, and a section groups related cards inside a Sections view. A good layout puts the household’s main questions first, keeps the same card in the same place on every device, and stays usable on a narrow screen.

[Dashboard composition and card features](../home-assistant/dashboard-composition.html) helps you choose between the four. This page owns each layout as an element: its options, its reading order and its limits.

This page covers:

- Section & View Layout
  - `<section>`
  - `hui-sections-view`
  - `hui-section`
  - `hui-masonry-view`
  - `hui-panel-view`
  - `hui-sidebar-view`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

A view has a header area for badges, then its layout. In a Sections view the layout is a row of sections, and each section is a column of cards on a grid. Masonry and Sidebar views have columns of cards. A panel view has one card.

A section has no title of its own. Open it with a [Heading card](card-and-section-header.html), which gives the section a visible name.

